    "answer": {
      "short": "No. Bases of logarithms cannot be negative.",
      "worked": "No. A real logarithm must have a base $b>0$, with $b\\ne1$. Although $(-5)^2=25$, the base $-5$ is negative, so $\\log_{-5}(25)$ is undefined as a real logarithm.",
